# Code health reports

One file per audit, named by date (`YYYY-MM-DD.md`), written by `/code-health`: the whole
codebase checked by area against the project's rules, with each finding's severity and place.
Run it every few features or before a milestone.

The reports are a record, not a to-do list: findings worth fixing become items in
[`../backlog/`](../backlog/README.md), and the report names them. One file per run means
parallel lanes never conflict over this folder.
